From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 02:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: drm: h713-afbd: attach the display to the IOMMU

DECD carries the IOMMU lifecycle in dec_frame_submit(): it attaches master 2
bypassing, then parks AFBD source 0, flips IOMMU_BYPASS 0x7c -> 0x78 and
unparks. Porting that shape to the KMS driver would be wrong, and the reason is
worth stating because it is not obvious by analogy.

DECD allocates no scanout buffers -- it only imports them -- so attaching it
while bypassing is harmless. This driver allocates its own framebuffers. The
moment the device joins an IOMMU paging domain, drm_gem_dma allocations return
IOVAs, and under bypass the hardware would scan an IOVA as a physical address:
garbage from boot, before any video frame exists. There is no bypassing phase
that works here, so there is no runtime flip to port. Translate from probe.

That is also simpler than DECD's arrangement. 0078 already programs the whole
video plane with source 0 disabled and enables it last, so there is no in-flight
scan to park across a transition, and the "never enable source 0 without a frame
address" rule is satisfied by construction.

Three pieces:

  - sun50i-iommu gains .get_resv_regions = iommu_dma_get_resv_regions, and
    binds the instance in domain_alloc_paging(). Reserved direct mappings are
    created before attach_device(), and both sun50i_table_flush() and the
    page-table allocator dereference sun50i_domain->iommu, so without the bind
    an IOMMU_RESV_DIRECT region NULL-derefs inside iommu_device_register().
    Both are lifted from the out-of-series 0075, which is not applied in the
    KMS configuration.

  - The adopted U-Boot logo at 0x6c100000 is identity-mapped, so the fetch that
    is already in flight at probe stays valid once master 2 translates. The
    phandle points at the device, not the IOMMU.

  - of_reserved_mem_device_init_by_name(..., "framebuffer") replaces the index-0
    lookup. of_iommu_get_resv_regions() only finds iommu-addresses on nodes the
    device lists in memory-region, but this driver consumed index 0 as its
    framebuffer pool -- listing the carveout there would have pointed dumb-buffer
    allocation at a no-map region. Naming the pool separates the two uses; with
    no "framebuffer" entry the lookup returns -ENODEV and the system CMA pool is
    used exactly as before.

The intended payoff beyond correctness: PRIME imports now resolve through the
IOMMU, so a physically fragmented Cedrus capture buffer coalesces into one
contiguous IOVA, which is what the plane's single-base-plus-stride fetch needs.
0078's contiguous-import restriction can be revisited once that is confirmed on
hardware; it is deliberately left in place here so this patch changes one thing.

UNTESTED ON HARDWARE. The risk is concentrated at probe: a bad identity map
faults the in-flight logo fetch and wedges AFBD for the boot. Recover by
rebooting over serial; U-Boot republishes the logo.

OUT OF SERIES. Apply after 0079.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/sun50i-iommu.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <linux/spinlock.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
 
+#include "dma-iommu.h"
 #include "iommu-pages.h"
 
 #define IOMMU_RESET_REG			0x010
@@ -730,6 +731,15 @@
 	if (!sun50i_domain)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * Reserved direct mappings are created before attach_device(), and both
+	 * sun50i_table_flush() and the page-table allocator dereference
+	 * sun50i_domain->iommu, which attach_domain() would normally set. Bind
+	 * the one H713 instance here or an IOMMU_RESV_DIRECT region NULL-derefs
+	 * inside iommu_device_register(). attach_domain() assigns the same value.
+	 */
+	sun50i_domain->iommu = sun50i_iommu_from_dev(dev);
+
 	sun50i_domain->dt =
 		iommu_alloc_pages_sz(GFP_KERNEL | GFP_DMA32, DT_SIZE);
 	if (!sun50i_domain->dt)
@@ -913,6 +923,7 @@
 static const struct iommu_ops sun50i_iommu_ops = {
 	.identity_domain = &sun50i_iommu_identity_domain,
 	.device_group	= generic_single_device_group,
+	.get_resv_regions = iommu_dma_get_resv_regions,
 	.domain_alloc_paging = sun50i_iommu_domain_alloc_paging,
 	.of_xlate	= sun50i_iommu_of_xlate,
 	.probe_device	= sun50i_iommu_probe_device,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -614,7 +614,14 @@
 	 * Point memory-region at a carveout to override that, e.g. to keep
 	 * scanout inside a known-good region; the ceiling comes with it.
 	 */
-	ret = of_reserved_mem_device_init(dev);
+	/*
+	 * By NAME, not index 0. The device must also list the adopted-scanout
+	 * carveout in memory-region so of_iommu_get_resv_regions() can find its
+	 * iommu-addresses and identity-map it; taking index 0 as the pool would
+	 * then point framebuffer allocation at a no-map region.
+	 */
+	ret = of_reserved_mem_device_init_by_name(dev, dev->of_node,
+						  "framebuffer");
 	if (ret && ret != -ENODEV)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "bad scanout memory-region\n");
 	dev_info(dev, "framebuffers from %s\n",
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@
 		framebuf_reserved: uboot-scanout@6c100000 {
 			reg = <0x6c100000 0x800000>;
 			no-map;
+			iommu-addresses = <&display 0x6c100000 0x800000>;
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -1701,6 +1702,17 @@
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_AFBD>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_BUS_DISP>;
 			clock-names = "clk_afbd", "clk_bus_disp";
+			/*
+			 * Master 2, translating from probe. Attaching at all
+			 * turns this driver's framebuffer allocations into
+			 * IOVAs, so the hardware must translate from the start
+			 * or it would scan an IOVA as a physical address. The
+			 * adopted logo it is already fetching is kept valid by
+			 * the identity map below.
+			 */
+			iommus = <&iommu 2 1>;
+			memory-region = <&framebuf_reserved>;
+			memory-region-names = "adopted-scanout";
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
